From 0237931e3b4480cf3453e98a916ed4f576d512a0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "suricata.lu" <suricata.lu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:23:33 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: enetc: Pass descriptor options to
 xsk_buff_get_metadata()

Patch 1094 in this folder, the stable backport of upstream commit
a6e4b9a6deb9 ("xsk: honor XDP_TX_METADATA in zero-copy path"), adds an
options argument to xsk_buff_get_metadata(), so that TX metadata is used
only when the descriptor sets XDP_TX_METADATA. It converts igc, mlx5 and
stmmac, but enetc gets its XSK TX metadata support from the NXP kernel
(93712d49a877 "LF-14857-13 net: enetc: add Tx timestamp to XDP zero copy
mode"), so it is not converted and no longer builds:

  error: too few arguments to function 'xsk_buff_get_metadata'

Pass the descriptor options as the other drivers do. When the option is
not set, the helper returns NULL and enetc already skips the metadata
request. Unlike mlx5 and stmmac, the completion data needs no extra
reset: enetc_clean_tx_ring() clears each tx_swbd after completion, so
tx_swbd->xsk_meta.tx_timestamp stays NULL for a descriptor without
metadata.

NXP lf-6.18.y still has the old helper, because upstream 6.18 does not
have this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/enetc/enetc.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/enetc/enetc.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/enetc/enetc.c
index 8c89f53464ad..9a91a5f6b678 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/enetc/enetc.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/freescale/enetc/enetc.c
@@ -2769,7 +2769,8 @@ static void enetc_xsk_descs_to_tx_ring(struct enetc_bdr *tx_ring,
 			first_txbd = txbd;
 			frm_len = tx_swbd->len;
 
-			meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, xsk_descs[j].addr);
+			meta = xsk_buff_get_metadata(pool, xsk_descs[j].addr,
+						     xsk_descs[j].options);
 			if (!meta)
 				goto no_metadata_req;
 
